# SYNTHETIC, written from RFC 1939 section 7. Not recorded from a server.
#
# TOP fetches headers plus a bounded number of body lines WITHOUT setting the seen flag, which
# RETR does. A first sync over a large maildrop must use this, or it marks the user's entire
# mailbox read in their webmail.
#
# The second body line is dot-stuffed: it was sent as "..signature" and is one line of content
# beginning with a single dot. Stuffing applies only at the START of a line, which is why the
# ".." here is at the line start and not inside the header value above.
S: +OK POP3 server ready
C: TOP 1 2
S: +OK top of message follows
S: From: ada@example.test
S: Subject: headers and two lines
S:
S: Hello there
S: ..signature follows
S: .
C: QUIT
S: +OK bye
DONE
